# Synthetic orchard block: 3x3 evenly spaced plants (4 m apart) on flat ground.
# Deliberately REPETITIVE - near-identical plants on a regular lattice - which
# is the case that defeats naive point-descriptor registration.
#
# A BLOCK rather than a single row on purpose: 4 plants in a line are
# genuinely ambiguous under an end-for-end flip, so a row cannot distinguish
# a correct match from a reversed one. A 2-D block has no such symmetry.
# Per-plant height/radius vary slightly, giving the weak features that let a
# matcher tell one plant from another.
# Generated with numpy, seed 20240607; see tests/e2e/auto-register-clouds.spec.ts.
